│  • Initializes structured_output_context.                          │
│  • Then executes the event loop cycle and yields events.           │
│  • Contains logic to redact user content based on events received  │
│    from model provider (guardrails).                               │
│                                                                    │
│  2 What is the relationship between this part of the code and the  │
│    bug?                                                            │
│                                                                    │
│  • The issue is that BeforeInvocationEvent is raised before        │
│    messages are appended to the agent.                             │
│  • This means hook handlers on BeforeInvocationEvent currently     │
│    cannot inspect or modify the input messages because the agent's │
│    messages are not updated yet.                                   │
│  • The request is to extend BeforeInvocationEvent to receive the   │
│    input messages and allow modification before messages are       │
│    appended.                                                       │
│  • Additionally, in _run_loop, the event should be raised with     │
│    messages passed, so hooks can modify the input messages before  │
│    appending.                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Given the issue description, what would be the intended         │
│    behavior of this part of the code?                              │
│                                                                    │
│  • Modify BeforeInvocationEvent invocation on line 647 to pass     │
│    both the agent and the messages parameter (input messages).     │
│  • This allows hook authors to see and edit incoming messages      │
│    early.                                                          │
│  • The event should be raised after message preparation and input  │
│    validation but before _append_messages.                         │
│  • The existing flow of yielding events and appending messages     │
│    should remain unchanged aside from this early hook              │
│    modification.                                                   │
│  • This prevents sensitive data from leaking into agent memory if  │
│    redaction/abort is needed on guardrail grounds.                 │
│                                                                    │
