│ The key problem is that the BeforeInvocationEvent hook is          │
│ currently invoked without knowledge of the input messages that are │
│ about to be processed by the agent, both in _run_loop() and        │
│ structured_output_async(). This means that hooks cannot redact or  │
│ validate input messages early enough.                              │
│                                                                    │
│ The fix involves two things:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Extend the BeforeInvocationEvent class to accept the messages   │
│    parameter as part of its event data, allowing hooks listening   │
│    to this event to access (and potentially modify) the invocation │
│    input messages.                                                 │
│  2 Adjust the agent code where BeforeInvocationEvent is invoked:   │
│     • In _run_loop() before firing BeforeInvocationEvent, pass the │
│       input messages so hooks receive them.                        │
│     • In structured_output_async(), move the construction of       │
│       combined messages (temp_messages) before firing the          │
│       BeforeInvocationEvent, then pass these messages to the       │
│       event.                                                       │
│                                                                    │
│ By doing so, hooks will have access to the messages exactly before │
│ the invocation proceeds, enabling early guardrails and input       │
│ redaction as intended.                                             │
│                                                                    │
